of July 2026\nEligibility\nThe candidate who have passed any Bachelor’s degree of minimum three years duration from any the recognized college / University of India as recognized by UGC with at least 50% marks (45% in case of candidates belonging to SC/ST category) in the qualifying examination are eligible to take MBA admission at ICCMRT.\nReservation\nAs per the norms of UP Government & AKTU, Lucknow.\nDirect Admission\nDirect admission into MBA Programme is also available against the vacant seats as per the AKTU approval. Students interested in MBA Direct Admission may call at 7355615114 / send their e-mail at principal@iccmrt.ac.in.\nDocuments Required for Admission\n1.  AKTU Seat Allotment Letter\n2.  Caste Certificate\n3.  Income Certificate\n4.  Domicile Certificate\n5.  Graduation Degree Certificate\n6.  Migration Certificate\n7.  Graduation Mark Sheets (All Semesters)\n8.  Intermediate Mark Sheet\n9.  High School Mark Sheet\n10. Gap Certificate (If Applicable)\n11. ID Proof (Aadhaar / Bank Pass Book)\n12. Four recent and identical Passport Size Photographs\nImportant Information & Rules\n- All admitted students must comply with the rules and regulations of the Institute, including the amendments (if any).\n- While on campus, every student is required to carry their identity card at all times.\n- Students must maintain regular attendance and punctuality in both academic and extra-curricular activities throughout the semester.\n- Students must come to the institute only in the prescribed uniform.\n- Students should exhibit responsible behavior and uphold decorum within the institute.\n- The candidate must check their eligibility before participating the entrance examination. If an ineligible candidate attempts the examination, he or she is entitled to claim admission under any circumstances.\n- During the reporting for admission, students must submit all their original documents, including marks sheets and certificates from their qualifying examination.\n- Students whose qualifying examination results have not been declared by the admission date, for any reason, will only be eligible for provisional admission.\n- Admitted students must submit all their original documents to MP Cell at the time of reporting. If any document is unavailable, they must submit the same within two months from the commencement of classes or at the time of AKTU Enrolment process, whichever is earlier. Failure to do so will result in the cancellation of their admission.\nTentative Date of MBA Class Commencement:  2^(nd) Week of August 2026\nMBA Fees\n  Semester     Tuition Fee    Refundable Caution Deposit   University Examination fees   Total\n  ------------ -------------- ---------------------------- ----------------------------- --------------\n  Semester 1   Rs. 49385.00   Rs. 8000.00                  Rs. 7500.00                   Rs. 64885.00\n  Semester 2   Rs. 49000.00   –                            –                             Rs. 49000.00\n  Semester 3   Rs. 49385.00   –                            Rs. 7500.00                   Rs. 56885.00\n  Semester 4   Rs. 49000.00   –                            –                             Rs. 49000.00\nMode of Payment\n1.  Students can make their payments to the Institute by Cash /Bank Draft / Cheques (out station cheques are not accepted) drawn in favour of the Director, ICCMRT payable at Lucknow.\n2.  Cash deposits of fee can be submitted at the Zila Sahkari Bank counter located at the institute using the prescribed fee deposit slip only.\n3.  Alternatively they can deposit the fee online through the Institute’s portal.\n4.  A copy of pay in slip of the fee deposited should be submitted at the MP Cell for future verification.\n5.  Booklets containing pay-in slips for this purpose shall be issued to the student during registration process. Duplicate fees booklet can be obtained from the MP Cell against written request along with a payment of Rs. 50.\n6.  Fees must be deposited latest by the due date declared by the Institute. Part payment of fees shall not be accepted. All dues must be cleared before obtaining admit card for end semester examinations.\n7.  Penalty will be charged at the rate of Rs.10/-per day for each day of late payment after the due date.\nMBA Specialization\nThe MBA Programme offered by the Institute offers dual specialization. Students may choose any two of the following subjects as their specialization during the second year. Specialization subjects offered: 1. Marketing Management, 2. Financial Management, 3. Human Resources Management, 4. Information Technology, 5. International Business, 6. Operations Management and 7. Cooperative Management.\nHostel Facility\nSeparate hostels for boys and girls are available within the Institute’s premises. The annual hostel fees including mess charges is Rs. 67,000/- per year payable in two equal instalments semester wise (i.e., Rs. 33500 per semester). Also students availing hostel facility should pay a refundable caution deposit of Rs. 5000 which will be reimbursed after completion of the course (or) at the time of leaving the hostel whichever is earlier\nFor Hostel Accommodation Students May Contact\n1.  Dr. Ram Komal Prasad, Associate Professor (Warden, Boys Hostel) :  9919360380\n2.  Dr. Smita Verma, Assistant Professor (Warden, Girls Hostel) :  9452101010\nContact Us\n467, Sector-21, Institutional Area, Ring Road, Indira Nagar LUCKNOW-226016\n0522-2716092\n7355615114, 9919360380\ninfo@iccmrt.ac.in\nOur Programme\n- MBA\n- BBA\n- B.Com (Hons)\nAcademics\n- Admissions\n- Faculty\n- Online Payment\n- Training\n- Contact Us\nImportant Links\n- AKTU University\n- Lucknow University\n- TSU\n- AICTE\n- UPESSC\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n© 2026 ICCMRT Lucknow.All Rights Reserved.\nInquiry Form\nQuick Enquiry\nSelect Course MBA BBA B.Com (Hons.)\nSubmit\n\n=== /bba/ ===\ninfo@iccmrt.ac.in | 0522-2716092\nOnline Payment Employee Login Enquiry\nAdmission Open 2026-27\n[Shri Narendra Modi]\nShri Narendra Modi\nHon'ble Prime Minister\nGovernment of India\n[Shri Amit Shah]\nShri Amit Shah\nMinister of Home Affairs\nGovernment of India\n[logo]\n[Yogi Adityanath]\nYogi Adityanath\nHon'ble Chief Minister\nUttar Pradesh\n[Shri JPS Rathore]\nShri JPS Rathore\nHon'ble Minister of State\n(Independent Charge)\nCo-Operative Govt. of U.P.\n- \n- About Us\n  - Overview\n  - Vision & Mission\n  - Management Committee\n  - Core Activities\n    - Education\n    - Research & Consultancy\n    - Training\n- Admissions\n  - Admissions\n  - MBA\n  - BBA\n  - B.Com (Hons)\n- Placement\n  - Placement\n  - Placement Cell\n- Faculty\n- Infrastructure\n- Training\n  - ADO/ ADCO Training\n  - ACABC Training\n  - Drone Remote Pilot Training\n- Gallery\n- Contact Us\nLATEST NEWS ^(New!)Students Interested in taking MBA/BBA Admission at ICCMRT, Lucknow through spot counselling may register at AKTU portal. Last Date 14.09.2026 || ^(New!)Admission Open for MBA/BBA/B.Com(Hons) 2026-27 || ^(New!)Certificate Courses of Tribhuvan Sahkari University || ^(New!)Drone Training Registration || ^(New!)Training for Officers/Employers ||\nBBA\nHome / BBA\nBBA Admission under LU (Intake: 60)\nThe BBA programme is under the affiliation of Lucknow University under NEP-2020.\nAdmission to 3 Year full- time BBA Programme (under NEP 2020) approved by the UGC and affiliated to the University of Lucknow (LU) is available in three modes namely;\n1.  LU Entrance Examination,\n2.  CUET-UG Examination and 3.  Direct Admission.\n1) Through LU Entrance\nStudents are admitted to the 3 Year full- time BBA Programme through the Entrance Test conducted by the University of Lucknow as per the following procedure;\n1.  Generate Lucknow University Registration Number (LURN) which is Mandatory for admission.Click the link LURN LINK (or)  https://lkounivadm.samarth.edu.in/index.php/registration/user-new/register\n- Appear in the Entrance Examination conducted by the University of Lucknow.\n- The MERIT LIST is generated based on your Entrance Examination performance.\n- Complete the choice filling for online counseling. Choose ICCMRT as your first choice.\n- Once the Seat Allotment is done by the LU, check your seat allotment status in the LU portal using your Candidate’s Login and Password.\n- Students who are allotted a seat at ICCMRT have to submit the Confirmation Fees of Rs. 4000 to the University through online.\n- Allotment cum Confirmation Letter shall be generated. Take the Printout and visit ICCMRT for further process.\n2) Through CUET-UG\nStudents who have appeared in the Common University Entrance Test (CUET-UG) conducted by National Testing Agency can also take admission in the BBA programme affiliated to the LU. The CUET-UG Candidates interested in BBA admission should;\n1.  Generate Lucknow University Registration Number (LURN) which is Mandatory for admission.Click the link LURN LINK (or)  https://lkounivadm.samarth.edu.in/index.php/registration/user-new/register\n- Report to ICCMRT with the LURN Registration Slip Printout– Mandatory. Also carry your CUET-UG result print out to complete the admission process.\n3) Direct Admission\nDirect admission into BBA Programme is also available against the vacant seats as per the LU approval. Students interested in BBA Direct Admission should;\n1.  Generate Lucknow University Registration Number (LURN) which is Mandatory for admission.Click the link LURN LINK (or)  https://lkounivadm.samarth.edu.in/index.php/registration/user-new/register\n2.  Report to ICCMRT with the LURNRegistration Slip Printout– Mandatory\nDocuments Required\n1.  LURN Seat Allotment Letter / Registration Slip\n2.  Caste Certificate\n3.  Income Certificate\n4.  Transfer Certificate\n5.  Intermediate Mark Sheet\n6.  High School Mark Sheet\n7.  ID Proof (Aadhaar Card)\n8.  Four recent and identical Passport Size Photographs\nEligiblity\nThe candidate who have passed 10 + 2 examination in any discipline, with at least 50% marks (45 % in case of candidate belonging to SC/ST category) in the qualifying examination are eligible to take BBA admission at ICCMRT.\nReservation\nAs per the norms of UP Government & University of Lucknow.\nFee Structure – BBA (2026-27)\n  ------------ ------------- ----------------- ---------------------- -----------\n  Semester     Tuition Fee   Caution Deposit   University Exam Fees   Total\n  Semester 1   Rs. 30000     Rs. 8000          Rs. 4000               Rs. 42000\n  Semester 2   Rs. 30000                       Rs. 4000               Rs. 34000\n  Semester 3   Rs. 30000                       Rs. 4000               Rs. 34000\n  Semester 4   Rs. 30000                       Rs. 4000               Rs. 34000\n  Semester 5   Rs. 30000                       Rs. 4000               Rs. 34000\n  Semester 6   Rs. 30000                       Rs. 4000               Rs. 34000\n  ------------ ------------- ----------------- ---------------------- -----------\nMode of Payment\n1.  Students can make their payments to the Institute by Cash /Bank Draft / Cheques (out station cheques are not accepted) drawn in favour of the Director, ICCMRT payable at Lucknow.\n2.  Cash deposits of fee can be submitted at the Zila Sahkari Bank counter located at the institute using the prescribed fee deposit slip only.\n3.  Alternatively they can deposit the fee online through the Institute’s portal.\n4.  A copy of pay in slip of the fee deposited should be submitted at the MP Cell for future verification.\n5.  Booklets containing pay-in slips for this purpose shall be issued to the student during registration process. Duplicate fees booklet can be obtained from the MP Cell against written request along with a payment of Rs. 50.\n6.  Fees must be deposited latest by the due date declared by the Institute. Part payment of fees shall not be accepted. All dues must be cleared before obtaining admit card for end semester examinations.\n7.  Penalty will be charged at the rate of Rs.10/-per day for each day of late payment after the due date.\nNote : \n- University examination fees has to be deposited by the students through online mode at university website.\n- The caution deposit is refundable to the students after their successful completion of the programme.\nBBA Admission under AKTU, Lucknow (Intake: 60)\nAdmission to 3 Year full- time BBA Programme (under NEP 2020) approved by the AICTE, New Delhi and affiliated to Dr. APJ Abdul Kalam Technical University (AKTU), Lucknow is available in two modes namely;\n1.  CUET-UG Examination Followed by AKTU Counselling\n2.  Direct Admission\n1) Through AKTU Counselling\nStudents are admitted to the 3 Year full- time BBA Programme (under NEP 2020) approved by the AICTE, New Delhi and affiliated to Dr. APJ Abdul Kalam Technical University (AKTU), Lucknow through Common University Entrance Test (CUET-UG)  conducted by National Testing Agency (NTA) followed by AKTU Counselling.\n1.  NTA Link for CUET UG:  National Testing Agency\n2.  AKTU Link for BBA Counselling:  Create an Account – Uttar Pradesh Technical Admission Counselling (UPTAC)\nTentative Date of AKTU Counselling:  1^(st) Week of July 2026\nTentative Date of BBA Class Commencement:  2^(nd) Week of August 2026\n2) Direct Admission\nDirect admission into BBA Programme is also available against the vacant seats as per the AKTU approval. Students interested in BBA Direct Admission may call at 7355615114 / send their e-mail at principal@iccmrt.ac.in\nDocuments Required for Admission\n1.  AKTU Seat Allotment Letter\n2.  Caste Certificate\n3.  Income Certificate\n4.  Transfer Certificate\n5.  Intermediate Mark Sheet\n6.  High School Mark Sheet\n7.  ID Proof (Aadhaar / Bank Pass Book)\n8.  Four recent and identical Passport Size Photographs\nEligibility\nThe candidate who have passed 10 + 2 examination in any discipline, with at least 50% marks (45 % in case of candidate belonging to SC/ST category) in the qualifying examination are eligible to take BBA admission at ICCMRT\nReservation\nAs per the norms of UP Government & AKTU, Lucknow.\nBBA Fees\nThe annual tuition fees for BBA is Rs. 60000 payable in two equal instalments semester wise. Students admitted in BBA programme also have to pay a refundable caution deposit of Rs. 8000 which will be reimbursed after their successful completion of the course.\n  -------------- -------------- ----------------- ---------------------- --------------\n  Semester       Tuition Fee    Caution Deposit   University Exam Fees   Total\n  Semester 1     Rs. 30000      Rs. 8000          Rs. 7500               Rs. 45500\n  Semester 2     Rs. 30000                        –                      Rs. 30000\n  Semester 3     Rs. 30000                        Rs. 7500               Rs. 37500\n  Semester 4     Rs. 30000                        –                      Rs. 30000\n  Semester 5     Rs. 30000                        Rs. 7500               Rs. 37500\n  Semester 6     Rs. 30000                        –                      Rs. 30000\n  -------------- -------------- ----------------- ---------------------- --------------\nMode of Payment\n1.  Students can make their payments to the Institute by Cash /Bank Draft / Cheques (out station cheques are not accepted) drawn in favour of the Director, ICCMRT payable at Lucknow.\n2.  Cash deposits of fee can be submitted at the Zila Sahkari Bank counter located at the institute using the prescribed fee deposit slip only.\n3.  Alternatively they can deposit the fee online through the Institute’s portal.\n4.  A copy of pay in slip of the fee deposited should be submitted at the MP Cell for future verification.\n5.  Booklets containing pay-in slips for this purpose shall be issued to the student during registration process. Duplicate fees booklet can be obtained from the MP Cell against written request along with a payment of Rs. 50.\n6.  Fees must be deposited latest by the due date declared by the Institute. Part payment of fees shall not be accepted. All dues must be cleared before obtaining admit card for end semester examinations.\n7.  Penalty will be charged at the rate of Rs.10/-per day for each day of late payment after the due date.\nHostel Facility\nSeparate hostels for boys and girls are available within the Institute’s premises. The annual hostel fees including mess charges is Rs. 67,000/- per year payable in two equal instalments semester wise (i.e., Rs. 33500 per semester). Also students availing hostel facility should pay a refundable caution deposit of Rs. 5000 which will be reimbursed after completion of the course (or) at the time of leaving the hostel whichever is earlier.\nFor Hostel Accommodation Students May Contact\n. Dr. Ram Komal Prasad, Associate Professor (Warden, Boys Hostel):   9919360380\n2. Dr. Smita Verma, Assistant Professor (Warden, Girls Hostel):   9452101010\nFor BBA Admission Enquiries\n- Dr. Richa Banerjee, Assistant Professor (Mob: 7408200056)\n-  Mr. Veelu Bhargava, Assistant Professor (Mob: 8960143956)\nContact Us\n467, Sector-21, Institutional Area, Ring Road, Indira Nagar LUCKNOW-226016\n0522-2716092\n\n=== /bcom/ ===\ninfo@iccmrt.ac.in | 0522-2716092\nOnline Payment Employee Login Enquiry\nAdmission Open 2026-27\n[Shri Narendra Modi]\nShri Narendra Modi\nHon'ble Prime Minister\nGovernment of India\n[Shri Amit Shah]\nShri Amit Shah\nMinister of Home Affairs\nGovernment of India\n[logo]\n[Yogi Adityanath]\nYogi Adityanath\nHon'ble Chief Minister\nUttar Pradesh\n[Shri JPS Rathore]\nShri JPS Rathore\nHon'ble Minister of State\n(Independent Charge)\nCo-Operative Govt. of U.P.\n- \n- About Us\n  - Overview\n  - Vision & Mission\n  - Management Committee\n  - Core Activities\n    - Education\n    - Research & Consultancy\n    - Training\n- Admissions\n  - Admissions\n  - MBA\n  - BBA\n  - B.Com (Hons)\n- Placement\n  - Placement\n  - Placement Cell\n- Faculty\n- Infrastructure\n- Training\n  - ADO/ ADCO Training\n  - ACABC Training\n  - Drone Remote Pilot Training\n- Gallery\n- Contact Us\nLATEST NEWS ^(New!)Students Interested in taking MBA/BBA Admission at ICCMRT, Lucknow through spot counselling may register at AKTU portal. Last Date 14.09.2026 || ^(New!)Admission Open for MBA/BBA/B.Com(Hons) 2026-27 || ^(New!)Certificate Courses of Tribhuvan Sahkari University || ^(New!)Drone Training Registration || ^(New!)Training for Officers/Employers ||\nB.Com (Hons)\nHome / B.Com (Hons)\nB.Com (Honours) Admission (Intake: 60)\nAdmission to 3 Year full- time B.Com (Honours) Programme (under NEP 2020) approved by the UGC and affiliated to the University of Lucknow (LU) is available in three modes namely;\n1.  LU Entrance Examination,\n2.  CUET-UG Examination\n3.  Direct Admission\n1) Through LU Entrance\nStudents are admitted to the 3 Year full- time B.Com (Honours) Programme through the Entrance Test conducted by the University of Lucknow as per the following procedure;\n1.  Generate Lucknow University Registration Number (LURN) which is Mandatory for admission.Click the link LURN LINK (or)  https://lkounivadm.samarth.edu.in/index.php/registration/user-new/register\n2.  Appear in the Entrance Examination conducted by the University of Lucknow.\n3.  The MERIT LIST is generated based on your Entrance Examination performance.\n4.  Complete the choice filling for online counseling. Choose ICCMRT as your first choice.\n5.  Once the Seat Allotment is done by the LU, check your seat allotment status in the LU portal using your Candidate’s Login and Password.\n6.  Students who are allotted a seat at ICCMRT have to submit the Confirmation Fees of Rs. 4000 to the University through online.\nAllotment cum Confirmation Letter shall be generated.Take the Printout and visit ICCMRT for further process\n2) Through CUET-UG\nStudents who have appeared in the Common University Entrance Test (CUET-UG) conducted by National Testing Agency can also take admission in the B.Com (Honours) Programme affiliated to the LU. The CUET-UG Candidates interested in B.Com (Honours) admission should;\n1.  Generate Lucknow University Registration Number (LURN) which is Mandatory for admission.Click the link LURN LINK (or)  https://lkounivadm.samarth.edu.in/index.php/registration/user-new/register\n2.  Report to ICCMRT with the LURNRegistration Slip Printout– Mandatory. Also carry your CUET-UG result print out to complete the admission process\n3) Direct Admission\nDirect admission into B.Com (Honours) Programme is also available against the vacant seats as per the LU approval. Students interested in B.Com (Honours) Direct Admission should;\n1.  Generate Lucknow University Registration Number (LURN) which is Mandatory for admission.Click the link LURN LINK (or)  https://lkounivadm.samarth.edu.in/index.php/registration/user-new/register\n2.  Report to ICCMRT with the LURNRegistration Slip Printout– Mandatory\nDocuments Required for Admission\n1.  LURN Seat Allotment Letter / Registration Slip\n2.  Caste Certificate\n3.  Income Certificate\n4.  Transfer Certificate\n5.  Intermediate Mark Sheet\n6.  High School Mark Sheet\n7.  ID Proof (Aadhaar Card)\n8.  Four recent and identical Passport Size Photographs\nEligibility\nThe candidate who have passed 10 + 2 examination in any discipline, with at least 60% marks (55 % in case of candidate belonging to SC/ST category) in the qualifying examination are eligible to take B.Com (Honours) admission at ICCMRT. Also, the student must have studied Commerce (or) Economics (or) Mathematics as one of the subjects at the intermediate level.\nReservation\nAs per the norms of UP Government & University of Lucknow.\nB.Com (Honours) Fees\n  ------------ ------------- ----------------- ---------------------- -----------\n  Semester     Tuition Fee   Caution Deposit   University Exam Fees   Total\n  Semester 1   Rs. 30000     Rs. 8000          Rs. 1750               Rs. 39750\n  Semester 2   Rs. 30000                       Rs. 1750               Rs. 31750\n  Semester 3   Rs. 30000                       Rs. 1750               Rs. 31750\n  Semester 4   Rs. 30000                       Rs. 1750               Rs. 31750\n  Semester 5   Rs. 30000                       Rs. 1750               Rs. 31750\n  Semester 6   Rs. 30000                       Rs. 1750               Rs. 31750\n  ------------ ------------- ----------------- ---------------------- -----------\nMode of Payment\n1.  Students can make their payments to the Institute by Cash /Bank Draft / Cheques (out station cheques are not accepted) drawn in favour of the Director, ICCMRT payable at Lucknow.\n2.  Cash deposits of fee can be submitted at the Zila Sahkari Bank counter located at the institute using the prescribed fee deposit slip only.\n3.  Alternatively they can deposit the fee online through the Institute’s portal.\n4.  A copy of pay in slip of the fee deposited should be submitted at the MP Cell for future verification.\n5.  Booklets containing pay-in slips for this purpose shall be issued to the student during registration process. Duplicate fees booklet can be obtained from the MP Cell against written request along with a payment of Rs. 50.\n6.  Fees must be deposited latest by the due date declared by the Institute. Part payment of fees shall not be accepted. All dues must be cleared before obtaining admit card for end semester examinations.\n7.  Penalty will be charged at the rate of Rs.10/-per day for each day of late payment after the due date\nHostel Facility\nSeparate hostels for boys and girls are available within the Institute’s premises. The annual hostel fees including mess charges is Rs. 67,000/- per year payable in two equal instalments semester wise (i.e., Rs. 33500 per semester). Also students availing hostel facility should pay a refundable caution deposit of Rs. 5000 which will be reimbursed after completion of the course (or) at the time of leaving the hostel whichever is earlier.\nFor Hostel Accommodation Students May Contact\n- Dr. Ram Komal Prasad, Associate Professor (Warden, Boys Hostel):   9919360380\n- Dr. Smita Verma, Assistant Professor (Warden, Girls Hostel):   9452101010\nFor B.Com (Honours) Admission Enquiries\n- Dr. Shikha Singh, Assistant Professor (Mob: 7355126990)\n- Ms. Sonal Khanna, Assistant Professor (Mob: 8604693163)\nContact Us\n467, Sector-21, Institutional Area, Ring Road, Indira Nagar LUCKNOW-226016\n0522-2716092\n7355615114, 9919360380\ninfo@iccmrt.ac.in\nOur Programme\n- MBA\n- BBA\n- B.Com (Hons)\nAcademics\n- Admissions\n- Faculty\n- Online Payment\n- Training\n- Contact Us\nImportant Links\n- AKTU University\n- Lucknow University\n- TSU\n- AICTE\n- UPESSC\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n© 2026 ICCMRT Lucknow.All Rights Reserved.\nInquiry Form\nQuick Enquiry\nSelect Course MBA BBA B.Com (Hons.)\nSubmit\n\n=== /training-2/ ===\ninfo@iccmrt.ac.in | 0522-2716092\nOnline Payment Employee Login Enquiry\nAdmission Open 2026-27\n[Shri Narendra Modi]\nShri Narendra Modi\nHon'ble Prime Minister\nGovernment of India\n[Shri Amit Shah]\nShri Amit Shah\nMinister of Home Affairs\nGovernment of India\n[logo]\n[Yogi Adityanath]\nYogi Adityanath\nHon'ble Chief Minister\nUttar Pradesh\n[Shri JPS Rathore]\nShri JPS Rathore\nHon'ble Minister of State\n(Independent Charge)\nCo-Operative Govt. of U.P.\n- \n- About Us\n  - Overview\n  - Vision & Mission\n  - Management Committee\n  - Core Activities\n    - Education\n    - Research & Consultancy\n    - Training\n- Admissions\n  - Admissions\n  - MBA\n  - BBA\n  - B.Com (Hons)\n- Placement\n  - Placement\n  - Placement Cell\n- Faculty\n- Infrastructure\n- Training\n  - ADO/ ADCO Training\n  - ACABC Training\n  - Drone Remote Pilot Training\n- Gallery\n- Contact Us\nLATEST NEWS ^(New!)Students Interested in taking MBA/BBA Admission at ICCMRT, Lucknow through spot counselling may register at AKTU portal. Last Date 14.09.2026 || ^(New!)Admission Open for MBA/BBA/B.Com(Hons) 2026-27 || ^(New!)Certificate Courses of Tribhuvan Sahkari University || ^(New!)Drone Training Registration || ^(New!)Training for Officers/Employers ||\nTraining\nHome / Training\nThe Institute carries out various training activities to different beneficiaries as follows:\n1. ADO/ ADCO Training: The Institute is an authorized center of training offering foundation / refresher / capacity building training to the Assistant Development Officers (ADOs) / Additional Development Officers (ADCOs) of the Cooperative Department. It offers training to various organizations / departments including Cooperative Auditors, UP State Mandi Parishad, NHRM, NHM and NGOs. Also it offers training to the Group A, B, C level officers of the Cooperative Department. Following is a snapshot of the training programmes offered by the Institute in the last five years.\n  ---------------------------- --------- --------- --------- --------- ---------\n  Year                         2022-23   2023-24   2024-25   2025-26   2026-27\n  Total No. of Organizations   25        28        24        24        6\n  Total No. of Trainees        1016      865       919       487       105\n  Total No. of Mandays         9178      3088      6877      7411      1295\n  ---------------------------- --------- --------- --------- --------- ---------\n2.  ACABC: The Institute is an approved Nodal Training Institute (NTI) to conduct the NABARD sponsored training of Agri-Clinics and Agri-Business Centre (AC & ABC) Scheme as approved by MANAGE, Hyderabad. Till now it has trained 352 Agri-graduate beneficiaries from 13 Batches under this scheme and helped more than hundreds of them to establish their own Agri- oriented business ventures.\n3. Drone Pilot Training: ICCMRT has been approved by DGCA-Directorate of Civil Aviation, Government of India as a Remote Pilot Training Organization (RPTO) to conduct Drone Pilot Training. On successfully completion of the training, the trainees are issued Drone Pilot Certificate which permit them to fly drone of respective category and class throughout India. In the year 2024-25 and 2025-26, ICCMRT has trained total 532 women members of WSHG and M-PACS. The Institute has further plan to train 266 more rural women members of M-PACS and WSHG in the year 2026-27. Along with the above ICCMRT has also started giving DGCA Approved Drone Pilot Training to the officials of Railway Protection Force and further plan to start Drone-MRO (Maintenance, Repair & Overhaul) training very soon.\nInstitute Highlights\n- Highly Qualified and Experienced Faculty Members\n- Better Placement Record (Maximum Package Rs. 12 LPA)\n- Air-Conditioned Class Rooms / Seminar Hall\n- Ultra-Modern Library and Computer Labs\n- State-of-the-Art Auditorium\n- Separate Hostels for Girls and Boys\n- Modern Gym and Sports Facilities\n- Wi-Fi Enable Campus\n- Well connected by Metro Station and Public Transport.\nContact Us\n467, Sector-21, Institutional Area, Ring Road, Indira Nagar LUCKNOW-226016\n0522-2716092\n7355615114, 9919360380\ninfo@iccmrt.ac.in\nOur Programme\n- MBA\n- BBA\n- B.Com (Hons)\nAcademics\n- Admissions\n- Faculty\n- Online Payment\n- Training\n- Contact Us\nImportant Links\n- AKTU University\n- Lucknow University\n- TSU\n- AICTE\n- UPESSC\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n© 2026 ICCMRT Lucknow.All Rights Reserved.\nInquiry Form\nQuick Enquiry\nSelect Course MBA BBA B.Com (Hons.)\nSubmit\n\n=== /training/ ===\ninfo@iccmrt.ac.in | 0522-2716092\nOnline Payment Employee Login Enquiry\nAdmission Open 2026-27\n[Shri Narendra Modi]\nShri Narendra Modi\nHon'ble Prime Minister\nGovernment of India\n[Shri Amit Shah]\nShri Amit Shah\nMinister of Home Affairs\nGovernment of India\n[logo]\n[Yogi Adityanath]\nYogi Adityanath\nHon'ble Chief Minister\nUttar Pradesh\n[Shri JPS Rathore]\nShri JPS Rathore\nHon'ble Minister of State\n(Independent Charge)\nCo-Operative Govt. of U.P.\n- \n- About Us\n  - Overview\n  - Vision & Mission\n  - Management Committee\n  - Core Activities\n    - Education\n    - Research & Consultancy\n    - Training\n- Admissions\n  - Admissions\n  - MBA\n  - BBA\n  - B.Com (Hons)\n- Placement\n  - Placement\n  - Placement Cell\n- Faculty\n- Infrastructure\n- Training\n  - ADO/ ADCO Training\n  - ACABC Training\n  - Drone Remote Pilot Training\n- Gallery\n- Contact Us\nLATEST NEWS ^(New!)Students Interested in taking MBA/BBA Admission at ICCMRT, Lucknow through spot counselling may register at AKTU portal. Last Date 14.09.2026 || ^(New!)Admission Open for MBA/BBA/B.Com(Hons) 2026-27 || ^(New!)Certificate Courses of Tribhuvan Sahkari University || ^(New!)Drone Training Registration || ^(New!)Training for Officers/Employers ||\nTraining\nHome / Training\nTraining, Research and Consultancy\nThe Institute undertakes research and consultancy assignments; conducts management and computer training for the officials of Govt. Departments, Corporations, and Co-operatives.\nTraining Infrastructure\nThe Institute is housed in its own integrated campus of 2.33 acres with a blend of architectural innovation, interiors and functional convenience. It has multi-storied  separate academic, administrative and hostel buildings having centrally air-conditioned seminar hall, library block, classrooms, well equipped with audio visual aid, tutorial rooms, computer labs and modern auditorium with latest Audio-Visual facilities. The campus is well surrounded by a boundary wall and has a secured environment.\nTraining Hall\nThe Institute has one centrally air-conditioned Training Hall with average carpet area of 132 Sqm. and with a seating capacity of 75-90 persons\nClass Rooms\nThe institute has 10 class rooms with average carpet area of 74 Sqm    well equipped with audio visual aid and 2 tutorial rooms with average carpet area of 36 Sqm. Institute has sufficient unused carpet area for converting into Modern Interactive board with Cabinet facility” classrooms for any future needs.\nComputer Center\nInstitute has two air-conditioned computer labs with carpet area of 200 Sqm with 150 Computers including 3 servers and 8 Laptops. The computer labs are equipped with the state-of-the-art computing resources to cater to the Academic / Training / Administrative needs of the Institute. The computer labs are equipped with LAN, internet and latest software. As there is a thrust on computer knowledge and expertise in the MBA & training programs, all labs are equipped with LCD for Presentation\nThe Institute carries out various training activities to different beneficiaries as follows;\n1. ADO/ ADCO Training\nThe Institute is an authorized center of training offering foundation / refresher / capacity building training to the Assistant Development Officers (ADOs) / Additional Development Officers (ADCOs) of the Cooperative Department. It offers training to various organizations / departments including Cooperative Auditors, UP State Mandi Parishad, NHRM, NHM and NGOs. Also it offers training to the Group A, B, C level officers of the Cooperative Department. Following is a snapshot of the training programmes offered by the Institute in the last five years.\n  ---------------------------- --------- --------- --------- --------- ---------\n  Year                         2022-23   2023-24   2024-25   2025-26   2026-27\n  Total No. of Organizations   25        28        24        24        6\n  Total No. of Trainees        1016      865       919       487       105\n  Total No. of Mandays         9178      3088      6877      7411      1295\n  ---------------------------- --------- --------- --------- --------- ---------\n2.  ACABC Training\nThe Institute is an approved Nodal Training Institute (NTI) to conduct the NABARD sponsored training of Agri-Clinics and Agri-Business Centre (AC & ABC) Scheme as approved by MANAGE, Hyderabad. Till now it has trained 352 Agri-graduate beneficiaries from 13 Batches under this scheme and helped more than hundreds of them to establish their own Agri- oriented business ventures.\n3. Drone Remote Pilot Training\nDrone Pilot Training is now mandatory to fly any drone above the weight of 250 gm. in India. Operating a drone without the mandatory certificate can result in heavy fines, confiscation of the drone and possibly even imprisonment.\n[]\n ICCMRT has been approved by DGCA-Directorate of Civil Aviation, Government of India as a Remote Pilot Training Organization (RPTO) to conduct Drone Pilot Training. On successfully completion of the training, the trainees are issued Drone Pilot Certificate which permit them to fly drone of respective category and class throughout India.\nAt ICCMRT we shall ensure trainees develop the Knowledge, Skills and Attitude to be a proficient drone pilot, not just for their current requirement, but also to graduate to higher category and more complex operations of drones. The successful completion of the training shall also open doors of opportunities for the trainees in the vast and rapidly growing drone industry. During the training, the trainees will get deeply immersed in the world of drones and the opportunities that come with it. They will be able to visualize the future of drones in India and the role they could play in it.\nGovernment of India visionary initiative under the “Sashakt Nari Viksit Bharat” programme, aimed at empowering   rural women by providing them with agricultural drones and the necessary training to operate them. The scheme is putting drone technology in the hands of women pilots from Self Help Groups (SHGs) to bring in the usage of Hi-tech modern technology in agricultural practices that shall result in remarkable increase in agricultural productivity along with financially empowering the rural women.\nIn order to strengthen the above prestigious scheme in the state, the Govt. of Uttar Pradesh has given the responsibility to ICCMRT to train the women members of M-PACS and WSHG (Women Self Help Group) to fly drones in the rural areas thus helping the farmers in various agriculture practices. In the year 2024-25 and 2025-26, ICCMRT has trained total 532 women members of WSHG and M-PACS. The Institute has further plan to train 266 more rural women members of M-PACS and WSHG in the year 2026-27. After successful completion of the training the rural women are being awarded with the DGCA-Director General of Civil Aviation, Government of India approved Drone Pilot License/Certificate.\nAlong with the above ICCMRT has also started giving DGCA Approved Drone Pilot Training to the officials of Railway Protection Force and further plan to start Drone-MRO (Maintenance, Repair & Overhaul) training very soon.\nHostel\nThe ICCMRT campus possesses well-furnished separate hostels for male and female trainees with adequate arrangements like Wi-Fi Connectivity, 24×7 Security, LED Televisions, Power backup generators, RO Water Filters, Water Coolers, Boilers, Indoor and Outdoor Sports facilities.\nFor Training Related Enquiries\n- Dr. Ram Komal Prasad, Associate Professor  (Mob: 9919360380)\n-  Mr. Anjum Zia Rizvi, Assistant Professor  (Mob: 9559593312)\nContact Us\n467, Sector-21, Institutional Area, Ring Road, Indira Nagar LUCKNOW-226016\n0522-2716092\n7355615114, 9919360380\ninfo@iccmrt.ac.in\nOur Programme\n- MBA\n- BBA\n- B.Com (Hons)\nAcademics\n- Admissions\n- Faculty\n- Online Payment\n- Training\n- Contact Us\nImportant Links\n- AKTU University\n- Lucknow University\n- TSU\n- AICTE\n- UPESSC\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n© 2026 ICCMRT Lucknow.All Rights Reserved.\nInquiry Form\nQuick Enquiry\nSelect Course MBA BBA B.Com (Hons.)\nSubmit\n\n=== /ado-adco-training/ ===\ninfo@iccmrt.ac.in | 0522-2716092\nOnline Payment Employee Login Enquiry\nAdmission Open 2026-27\n[Shri Narendra Modi]\nShri Narendra Modi\nHon'ble Prime Minister\nGovernment of India\n[Shri Amit Shah]\nShri Amit Shah\nMinister of Home Affairs\nGovernment of India\n[logo]\n[Yogi Adityanath]\nYogi Adityanath\nHon'ble Chief Minister\nUttar Pradesh\n[Shri JPS Rathore]\nShri JPS Rathore\nHon'ble Minister of State\n(Indep